In the financial year 2009-10, there was a change in FDI regulation relating to sectoral cap which enabled the GSPL to acquire some shares in SBPL and thereby increase its indirect share holding in VIL and accordingly, on 7-4-2009, CGP and person nominated by GSPL entered into an agreement relating to transfer of 4900 shares SBPL which constitute 49 per cent stake by the AS to CGP. The value of 49 per cent shares of SBPL was worked out at Rs.533 crores, i.e., 49 per cent of Rs.1088 crores for which necessary approval from FIPB was sought and was also granted. [Para 51]

The long-term capital gain on transfer of said shares was offered for tax in the financial year 2010-11 by the assessee. In the financial year 2012-13, 'right issue' of 38.24 crores equity shares of Rs.10 each at par was issued by SBPL which was subscribed by the existing shareholders, i.e. AS and CGP in full. Accordingly, the assessee subscribed 19.50 crores shares and CGP subscribed to 18.74 crores in the existing ratio of 51:49. In pursuance of such acquisition, '4th Supplement to the Framework Agreement' was entered between the AS, SBPL, GSPL and various other companies to provide similar call/put option for the sale of newly issued right shares by the AS to GSPL at pre-agreed lump sum consideration of Rs.300 crores.[Para 52]
